.TH CHTTPCLI_SET_ENGINE_MEM_MGMT_PROCS 3 "2026-07-14" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpcli_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs \- set custom memory management for the allocations of the async engine of chttpclient
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpcli_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs(ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mp);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Every chttpcli instance in this process shares one ccol_event_loop
reactor for its Tier 2 and Tier 3 work. This function sends every
allocation of that reactor (the registration table, the dispatch state
of each connection, the worker pool for DNS and for connect, and more)
to the malloc, free, calloc and realloc in mp, in the same way as the
memory management procs of every other module in this library. An mp
of NULL puts the default allocator back.

Each chttpcli instance also has an allocator for its own requests and
connections, which you set with ccol_create_chttpclient_mp, following
the usual _mp convention. This function is independent of it, and
affects only the construction of the one shared reactor.

You can call this function only at two times: before the reactor ever
starts in this process (that is, before the first call to
chttpclient_do_async or to chttpclient_do_async_streaming anywhere),
or after the engine stops completely, which happens after every async
user of a chttpcli drops its reference and the automatic teardown
finishes. The reactor of chttpsvr_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs usually
lives for the whole process, but this engine starts and stops on its
own with the Tier 2 and Tier 3 traffic, so the window for this call
comes back again and again instead of being one chance at the start of
the process.

If mp is not NULL, all four function pointers in it (malloc, free,
calloc and realloc) must be set.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success, if the call succeeds.
ccol_invalid_args, if mp is not NULL but holds a function pointer that
    is NULL.
ccol_not_permitted, while the engine runs. Wait for the engine to stop
    completely first.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpcli_set_engine_logger (3),
.BR chttpcli_set_engine_num_reactor_threads (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_async (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_pooled (3),
.BR chttpsvr_set_engine_mem_mgmt_procs (3)
